# Agents. Worktrees are created in here and live inside the repo, so without
# this every parallel session shows up as untracked clutter in every other one.
# Ignored wholesale rather than by name, because whatever a future tool drops
# beside them is local state too — sessions, worktrees, caches. The exceptions
# are the things the repo shares on purpose rather than accumulates, and they
# share one test: something only one machine has is a convention the next agent
# will not follow. That covers the permission allowlist and the hooks beside it,
# the skills and subagents that encode this repo's own review and workflow rules,
# the path-scoped rules that keep those out of every session's context, and the
# scripts a dispatched agent is told to run.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/scripts/
